    "updated_at": "2026-04-08T17:47:30Z",
    "body": "The flow of logic is something akin to:\n\ndialog.requestClose(); https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#dialog-request-close\n- Step 4 enables the dialogs close watcher.\n- Step 7 goes into close watcher code:\n\nClose watcher request code https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#close-watcher-request-close\n\nStep 7 sets is_running_cancel_action to true \nStep 8 fires a cancel event which then reenters dialog.requestClose();\n\nThis goes through the same as above but inside close watcher it early returns at Step 3.\nThen Step 8 *disables* the close watcher.\n\nNow the logic from the original entrance into close watchers continues and inside of close watcher close Step 2 early returns because the close watcher is now *disabled*.\n\nLeading to an open dialog.\n\nThis feels weird, but I'm also not sure it's a big deal because this is edge case handling for something authors shouldn't be doing.",
